build: 2026-07-01 v10.77.0 (Video — record the bio-reactive visual, WITH sound; crash fix)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie (deployed via deploy branch, commit 37b2838)
notesT: NEW — you can now RECORD your bio-reactive visual as a shareable .mp4 WITH the music.
  Open the fullscreen immersive visual, tap the new Record button (top bar, turns red), let the
  music + biofeedback run, tap Stop → a share sheet appears with the finished .mp4 (H.264 video
  + AAC audio). The recorded picture is the Metal visual your pulse drives (NOT the rPPG
  finger-camera), so there's no interference with pulse measurement.
  CRASH FIX (was crashing on Record in build 2092): recording the audio no longer taps the audio
  engine's OUTPUT node — AVFAudio forbids that (the "_isInput" assertion, an immediate crash).
  Instead we reuse the always-on RetroCapture ring buffer (the last ~30 s of the master mix),
  read-only, no new tap → no crash.
  Under the hood: VisualRecorder blits the rendered Metal frame → H.264 (VideoRecorder);
  AudioEngine.captureRecentMixAudio pulls the matching tail of the mix from the RetroCapture ring;
  VideoMuxer combines them via AVAssetExportSession into one mp4, trimmed to the shorter track.
  KNOWN LIMITS this build: A/V sync is best-effort (~tens of ms, not sample-accurate); only the
  Metal visual records (the spectrum-donut mode doesn't yet); no trim UI yet.
  Test 10.77: fullscreen visual → Record → play music/bio → Stop → share the mp4 → confirm it
  plays with sound and the picture matches, AND that tapping Record no longer crashes.
